## Workflow (s3.1.0 — server-only, paid before live)

**Every write to `spotAdCampaigns` goes through Functions** (`functions/ad-functions.js`, pure helpers in `functions/ad-core.js`). Firestore rules deny all client writes to `spotAdCampaigns`, `adCampaignPrivate`, `adStats*`, `adSettings`, `adInvoices`, `adInvoiceAccounts`, `adIntakeSubmissions`, `adAuditLogs`, `adPosterDelegations`, `promotionGroups`. Storage `adMedia/{uid}/…` is owner-create, image (< 8 MB) or video (< 60 MB) content types only; `adIntake/…` is Functions-only; legacy `spotAds/{uid}/…` stays image-only.

1. Poster composes in the shared composer `floqr-ad-composer.js` (My Profile → **Ad Campaigns** via `patron-ad-campaigns.js`; Club Admin → **In-App Marketing** via `admin-spot-ads.js`). Poster identity comes from `getAdPostingIdentities`.
2. `createAdCampaign` validates (`validateCampaignInput`), re-inspects uploaded media server-side (`inspectAdMedia`: magic bytes; MP4/MOV `mvhd` duration ≤ **30 s** + 0.5 s tolerance; image ≤ 8 MB, video ≤ 60 MB) → `status: awaiting_payment`.
3. Payment: `payg` / `subscription` → Stripe Checkout (`orderType: "adCampaign"`, `serviceOrders`). `invoice` only when `adInvoiceAccounts/{posterKey}.enabled` → straight to `pending_approval` with `paymentStatus: invoiced`.
4. Stripe webhook / `confirmFloqrCheckoutSession` → `fulfillAdOrder` → `paymentStatus: paid`, `status: pending_approval`, `adInvoices/{invoiceNumber}` written, Master Admin Inbox row (`#adApprovalQueue`).
5. `onAdInvoiceCreated` sends the invoice to the payer (Inbox + email; SMS/WhatsApp reply for intake) with `ad-invoice.html` link.
6. Master Admin **Approve** (`approveAdCampaign`, SOS2FA) — refused unless paid / invoiced / waived (`canApprove`); waive needs a reason. Sets flight `startsAtMs`/`endsAtMs` → `status: active`.
7. `expireAdCampaigns` (hourly) flips past-`endsAtMs` to `expired`, prunes dedupe + stale intake.
8. Patron Search splash / Mingl / Gist / RydR read `active` docs via `FLOQRAdCampaigns` (servable = `active` | `live` only).

Statuses: `awaiting_payment`, `pending_approval`, `active`, `paused`, `rejected`, `expired`, `cancelled`. Paid states: `paid`, `invoiced`, `waived`. Reject with a paid Stripe order offers a refund.

Public fields live on `spotAdCampaigns`; contact name/email/phone + Stripe ids live in `adCampaignPrivate/{id}` (Master Admin read only).

## Who may post (poster identities)

`resolvePosterIdentities` → `{posterType, posterId, label, via, key}`; `posterKey = "{type}:{id}"`.

| posterType | Source |
|---|---|
| `club` | Club Admin of the venue (`adminUids`, `masterAdminUids`, `adminEmails`, `clubAdminAssignments`) **or** a delegated **Club Ad Poster** (`adPosterDelegations`, role **Club Ad Poster** added to `users.approvedRoles` + `adPosterClubIds`, set by Club Admin via `setClubAdPoster`) |
| `promotionGroup` | Member with `canPostAds` in `promotionGroups` (owner manages members via `upsertPromotionGroup` / `setPromotionGroupMember`) |
| `promoter`, `dj`, `mediaCreator` | Approved role text on `users.approvedRoles` / `roles` |
| `serviceMember` | `IsServiceMember` / legacy aliases |
| `business` | `accountType: business` |
| `floqq` | FloqQ / ticketing role or Master Admin (ticketed events) |
| `thirdParty` | SMS / WhatsApp intake only |

## Splash rotation (restored s3.1.0)

Search category / club tap → 5 s splash (`patron-app.js` `renderSplashAd` → `#adCreative`): club logo, FLOQR logo, “Powered by Papi and Social OS”, loading text **plus** the picked creative (image or muted looping video ≤ 30 s), Sponsored badge, Learn more. Picker: `FLOQRAdCampaigns.pick(slot)` scores targeting (gender, min/max age, tags), paid real campaigns outrank packaged demos, advertiser-diversified rotation. Controls in `adSettings/global`: `splashEnabled`, `splashSeconds` (3–10, default 5), `showDemoAds`, `packagedAdsEnabled`.

## Measurement (s3.1.0 — real, not formulas)

`floqr-ad-tracking.js` → callable `recordAdEvent({campaignId, event: impression|click, slot, packaged})`. Server: only servable campaigns (or packaged ids) count; per-viewer dedupe window (`adEventDedupe`) + throttle (`adEventThrottle`); increments `adStats/{id}` (`impressions`, `clicks`, `bySlot`) and `adStatsDaily/{id}_{yyyymmdd}`. CTR = clicks / impressions from those docs. The old `Math.max(10000, …)` × 3.5 % estimate is removed (test-guarded).

Clear: `resetAdStats({campaignId | "all", reason})` — SOS2FA, reason, audited (`ad.stats_reset` with before snapshot). “Clear all” requires typing CLEAR in the UI.

## Master Admin → Ad Management (tab group)

`master-admin.html` tab group `adManagement`, mounted by `master-ad-management.js` after SOS2FA unlock (`floqr:sos2fa-unlocked`):

| Subtab | Panel id | Does |
|---|---|---|
| Approval queue | `adApprovalQueue` | Awaiting payment + pending: edit (copy, link, demographics, dates via `updateAdCampaign`), Approve, Waive & approve, Mark invoice paid, Reject (+ refund) |
| Live campaigns | `adLiveCampaigns` | Pause / Resume / End (`setAdCampaignState`), clear stats per campaign |
| Stats | `adStatsPanel` | Measured totals, per-campaign table, 14-day daily; Clear one / Clear all |
| SMS & WhatsApp intake | `adIntakePanel` | Intake rows (masked phone, media, status), purge expired / unpaid (`purgeAdIntake`) |
| Settings | `adSettingsPanel` | `setAdSettings`, invoice accounts (`setAdInvoiceAccount`), audit log (`adAuditLogs`) |
| Packaged demos | `adCampaignManagement` | Legacy packaged demo editor (localStorage overrides only) |

All Master callables: `assertSos2faSession` (scope `entityManagement`), reason ≥ 8 chars where state changes, audited to `adAuditLogs`.

## SMS / WhatsApp third-party intake

1. Advertiser texts / WhatsApps a flyer (JPG/PNG/GIF/WebP) or video ≤ 30 s (or `AD`) to the FLOQR number. Twilio → `adIntakeWebhook` (dedicated number) or `messagingInboundWebhook` (shared number hook). Twilio signature validated; STOP/START/HELP honored (`adIntakeOptOuts`); daily cap per phone (`maxIntakePerPhonePerDay`); `intakeEnabled` kill switch.
2. Media downloaded from Twilio only, inspected, stored at `adIntake/{id}/creative.*`. `adIntakeSubmissions/{sha256(token)}` (phone hashed + masked; token never stored).
3. Reply (via `sendTwilioMessagesApi` — compliance rows) with `ad-submit.html?v=&t=<token>` (72 h).
4. `ad-submit.html` (public, `data-floqr-public`): title, copy, link, placement, payment mode (`payg` | `subscription`; invoice refused), run days, start date, **demographics** (age, gender, cities, countries, interests, music), contact → `startAdIntakeCheckout` → Stripe → `confirmAdIntakePayment` → campaign `pending_approval` (`posterType: thirdParty`, `source: intake`) + invoice link `ad-invoice.html?t=`.
5. Master Admin edits demographics in the queue before approve.

WhatsApp replies are session replies inside the 24 h window the advertiser opened; production delivery still needs the production WhatsApp sender (see `whatsapp-twilio-incomplete.mdc`).

## Invoices

`adInvoices/{invoiceNumber}` (`FLQ-AD-…`, `buildInvoiceLines`). `getAdInvoice` by intake token (public) or by invoice number (payer / poster / Master Admin). `ad-invoice.html` prints.

## Pricing (DOOH-informed)

US DOOH / programmatic digital out-of-home CPM commonly ~$5–25; high-attention interstitial / takeover inventory sits toward the top. In-app feed native CPM often ~$5–12.

| Placement | Package | Justification |
|---|---|---|
| Inline | **$45 / 7 days** | Interruptive, feature-path attention comparable to mid DOOH interstitial (~$12–18 CPM × ~250–400 expected impressions) |
| Mingl Gist | **$25 / 7 days** | Scroll-native, higher volume / lower interrupt (~$6–10 CPM × similar volume) |

Targeted audience vs **all patrons**: same package price in v1 (targeting is included). Geo/interest premium may be added later.

Constants: `window.FLOQRAdPricing` in `floqr-ad-pricing.js`.

Payment modes (invoice / subscription / pay-as-you-go): see `design-notes-ad-campaigns-payment-modes.mdc`.

## Targeting

- `targetMode: "all"` — eligible for any signed-in patron (age gates still apply)
- `targetMode: "targeted"` — `targetTags` from patron datapoints (city, music, nightlife, food, beverages, hobbies, travel, lookingToMeet, gender, ageRange)

### Master Admin editors (human forms → stored structure)

Operators must **not** edit raw JSON. Ad Campaign Mgmt uses plain inputs:

| UI | Stored field | Guard rails |
|---|---|---|
| Match tags (comma-separated) | `targetTags: string[]` | trim; max 80 tags × 80 chars |
| Tag categories (Category + tags rows) | `campaignDatapoints: [{category, tags}]` | category + ≥1 tag per kept row; optional clarity only |
| Required match groups (label + multi-select profile fields + tags) | `requiredTargetGroups: [{label, fields, tags}]` | each group needs ≥1 field and ≥1 tag; hard AND across groups |

Save serializes forms via `normalizeDatapoints` / `normalizeRequiredGroups` into `localStorage` overrides (`floqrAdCampaignOverrides:v28.99`) for packaged demos — it does **not** rewrite Firestore `spotAdCampaigns` docs. Scoring still uses `targetTags` + required groups — categories are operator-facing organization.

**Preview creative** toggles a sandboxed flyer/HTML preview on pending and live cards (`mountCreativePreview`). HTML ads stay in `sandbox=""` iframes — never host `innerHTML`.

### Card badge (Status · Shows on)

Top-right of each campaign card uses human labels — never raw `preview · shoutout`:

| Part | Example | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| **Status** | Demo (not live) / Live / Awaiting approval | Lifecycle. `preview` status → **Demo (not live)** packaged test creative, not a paid approved flight |
| **Shows on** | ShoutOut path / Inline package / Mingl Gist package | `placementType` when set; else first `slots[]` entry mapped to a feature path |

Helpers: `campaignStatusLabel`, `campaignPathLabel`, `campaignBadgeHtml`. Hover/`title` + FloqAi `help-ad-campaign-status-badge` explain the badge. **Preview creative** is a separate button.

## Why patrons only saw Zebbies

Packaged DC spots often have **empty** `targetTags`, so they always pass scoring, while brand demos with tags fail when the patron profile has no overlap. Rotation then collapses onto the DC pack (Zebbies frequently). Fix: honor `targetMode: "all"`, diversify rotation by advertiser, and include non-DC `active` creatives with empty tags / all-mode.

